INSERT INTO test_step (id, step_name, step_description, expected_result, script_id, created_date, updated_at) VALUES ('f8e5abf5-0954-4884-8034-5668fe816dfe', 'STEP 1', '1. For writable parameters, check if L2 SET use-case is defined.
2. For those parameters with L2 SET use-case defined, get the initial value. Return failure if get operation fails.
3. Then determine the value to be SET from the permissible value ranges of SET values.
4. For the SET value determined, get the initial values of defined dependencies if any. Return failure if any of the get operations fail.
5. Execute the SET operation of the parameters after all dependencies are SET successfully. If any of the SET operations fail, return failure.
6. Confirm with GET operation if all values are SET properly. Return failure if any SET value did not reflect in GET.
7. Now, revert the parameter to the initial value after identifying all revert dependencies and setting them. Return failure if any SET operations fail during revert or if SET does not reflect in GET.', 'All L2 SET operations should be successful and the corresponding use-cases under XDNS module should be validated successfully.', '018989ac-e59d-449a-b99c-3608313d8a03', '2026-03-19 06:39:39.381399', '2026-03-19 06:39:39.381401');
DELETE FROM test_step WHERE script_id = '735e21fa-7a2c-4c61-92b5-fca22dbe3447';
INSERT INTO test_step (id, step_name, step_description, expected_result, script_id, created_date, updated_at) VALUES ('f9f8c47f-beb8-4b5b-8b58-d894b06af069', 'STEP 1', '1. Perform a getnames (GETN) recursive walk from the top level objects under the TELEMETRY module all the way until the leaf nodes.
2. Cross check if all the expected parameters are found under component.
3. Return success if all parameters are found. Else, return failure and publish the failed parameters list.', 'All the required namespaces under TELEMETRY module should exist.', '735e21fa-7a2c-4c61-92b5-fca22dbe3447', '2026-03-19 06:39:36.869723', '2026-03-19 06:39:36.869725');
DELETE FROM test_step WHERE script_id = '89eea796-0bef-4a3d-80fe-39cb98974fb7';
INSERT INTO test_step (id, step_name, step_description, expected_result, script_id, created_date, updated_at) VALUES ('fb230ba1-7b1a-4174-8830-58818f5eb6f9', 'STEP 1', '1. Identify all table objects of type "writableTable" that are non-rigid under the TDM module which are applicable for the device platform under test.
2. Perform an add table row operation and ensure that it returns success, if not collect the failed table name.
3. After a successful add table operation, check if all expected parameters are found under that table instance using a getnames operation (GETN). If not collect the failed table name.
4. If the add table row operation is success, proceed to delete the same added table row instance.
5. Check if the delete table row operation is success, if not collect the failed table name.
6. Return success if add table row, getnames operation under the added table instance and delete table row operations are all success. Else, return failure and publish the failed tables.', 'Adding and deleting rows to/from non-rigid writable tables should be success and the added table instance should have all the required parameters under it for TDM module.', '89eea796-0bef-4a3d-80fe-39cb98974fb7', '2026-03-19 06:39:39.152092', '2026-03-19 06:39:39.152093');
DELETE FROM test_step WHERE script_id = 'b22545a9-ba3c-4ab7-970a-4b1db669d2f2';
INSERT INTO test_step (id, step_name, step_description, expected_result, script_id, created_date, updated_at) VALUES ('fb71f12f-d891-4c89-a76c-e6503ec0e610', 'STEP 1', '1. For all parameters under the MTA Agent module which are applicable for the device platform under test, perform a GET operation using WebPA protocol.
2. Initiate a SET operation on all those parameters with the same value retrieved using the previous GET operation but with an incorrect datatype using WebPA protocol.
3. The parameter will be write type compliant if the SET operations fail with the expected error code.
4. Return success if all applicable parameters are write type compliant. Else, return failure and publish the failed parameters list.', 'Writable parameters in MTA Agent module should throw the expected error code when a SET operation is attempted on it with an invalid parameter type using WebPA protocol.', 'b22545a9-ba3c-4ab7-970a-4b1db669d2f2', '2026-03-19 06:39:34.530971', '2026-03-19 06:39:34.530973');
DELETE FROM test_step WHERE script_id = 'ee8af126-b648-4dc8-a8a9-6e27d3f1c288';
INSERT INTO test_step (id, step_name, step_description, expected_result, script_id, created_date, updated_at) VALUES ('fc705572-ee58-42e1-86e5-622b6777eabd', 'STEP 1', '1. Under the VLANMANAGER module, identify all the parameters with the read-only access type which are applicable for the device platform under test.
2. For all such parameters, perform a SET operation with a new value in line with the parameters''s datatype.
3. Check if the SET operation returns a FAILURE with the expected error code.
4. Return success if all read-only parameters fail with the expected return code. Else, return failure and publish the failed parameters list.', 'Setting the "read-only" TR-181 DML parameters under the VLANMANAGER module should return error code.', 'ee8af126-b648-4dc8-a8a9-6e27d3f1c288', '2026-03-19 06:39:41.423052', '2026-03-19 06:39:41.423053');
DELETE FROM test_step WHERE script_id = '07746ac2-4c81-4fb2-b13b-256c92ed767f';
INSERT INTO test_step (id, step_name, step_description, expected_result, script_id, created_date, updated_at) VALUES ('fd5451fe-25c3-46e7-bd33-aa4b95771c14', 'STEP 1', '1. For all parameters under the MISC module which are applicable for the device platform under test, perform a GET operation using WebPA protocol.
2. Initiate a SET operation on all those parameters with the same value retrieved using the previous GET operation but with an incorrect datatype using WebPA protocol.
3. The parameter will be write type compliant if the SET operations fail with the expected error code.
4. Return success if all applicable parameters are write type compliant. Else, return failure and publish the failed parameters list.', 'Writable parameters in MISC module should throw the expected error code when a SET operation is attempted on it with an invalid parameter type using WebPA protocol.', '07746ac2-4c81-4fb2-b13b-256c92ed767f', '2026-03-19 06:39:36.482208', '2026-03-19 06:39:36.482209');
DELETE FROM test_step WHERE script_id = '06db4b5a-decd-4c65-8af9-816929c6be3c';
INSERT INTO test_step (id, step_name, step_description, expected_result, script_id, created_date, updated_at) VALUES ('fe7cc616-6761-4c94-9760-45d5e22a01fd', 'STEP 1', '1. Identify all table objects of type "staticTable" under the LMLite module which are applicable for the device platform under test.
2. For all applicable Static Tables, get the current number of rows.
3. For Static Tables with row count greater than 0, perform a delete table row operation of the last table row instance.
4. Check if the delete table row operation fails with the expected error code for Static Tables.
5. Return success if rows do not get deleted from the applicable Static Tables. Else, return failure and publish the failed tables.', 'Deleting rows from static table objects under LMLITE module should return the expected errorcode.', '06db4b5a-decd-4c65-8af9-816929c6be3c', '2026-03-19 06:39:40.825231', '2026-03-19 06:39:40.825232');
DELETE FROM test_step WHERE script_id = '11dae718-431b-4cd7-91bf-a31df59a358d';
INSERT INTO test_step (id, step_name, step_description, expected_result, script_id, created_date, updated_at) VALUES ('ff39ccb5-3ac5-4c0c-9127-4f004ee39c68', 'STEP 1', '1. For all parameters under the Advanced Security module which are applicable for the device platform under test, perform a GET operation using WebPA protocol.
2. Initiate a SET operation using WebPA protocol on all those parameters with the same value retrieved using the previous GET operation and with the parameter''s datatype.
3. The parameter will be write-access compliant if the SET operation does not fail with read-only error code.
4. Return success if all applicable parameters are write-access compliant. Else, return failure and publish the failed parameters list.', 'Writable parameters in Advanced Security module should not throw read-only error code when a SET operation is attempted on it using WebPA protocol.', '11dae718-431b-4cd7-91bf-a31df59a358d', '2026-03-19 06:39:39.459456', '2026-03-19 06:39:39.459457');
DELETE FROM script_device_type WHERE script_id = '017f3a42-1d83-4548-a70d-bfe88bc5f711';
